@notice Redeem shares for assets - user receives value of redeemed shares or maximum possible
@dev Burns specified shares and returns corresponding assets. If user tries to redeem more
     shares than they have, automatically adjusts to their maximum available shares.
     Treasury fees are deducted from user's remaining balance by burning additional shares.
@param shares The number of vault shares to burn (auto-adjusted if exceeds balance)
@param receiver The address that will receive the asset value
@param owner The address that owns the shares being burned
@return assets The amount of assets transferred to receiver (based on actual shares redeemed)
@dev CRUCIAL Fee Implementation:
     - User receives: Asset value of redeemed shares (auto-adjusted if necessary)
     - Treasury fee is deducted from user's remaining vault balance
     - Additional shares are burned to cover treasury fees (if user has sufficient shares)
     - Example: Request 2000 shares but only have 1000 → redeems 1000 shares
     - Auto-adjustment considers both share availability and treasury fee requirements

